HST Office: an .xlsx saved by HST Office keeps its cached formula results when it is opened again.

hst-version-everywhere.patch writes the generator as "HSTOffice/<release>$<OS>_<ARCH>" instead of "LibreOffice/...",
and maps it back for OpenDocument files (xmloff xmlmetai.cxx), but the .xlsx import only trusts the cached results
of files whose generator starts with "Microsoft" or "LibreOffice" (WorkbookHelper, mbGeneratorKnownGood). For HST's
own files every formula with a text result was calculated again on open, and a workbook whose numeric results are
all 0 was recalculated in full; the reload of upstream testTdf147088 showed the recalculated U+FFFF instead of the
saved result. "HSTOffice/" is a known generator now, like the engine it is built on.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: make CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_export_test4 (testTdf147088).
---
--- a/sc/source/filter/oox/workbookhelper.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/filter/oox/workbookhelper.cxx
@@ -569,7 +569,10 @@ void WorkbookGlobals::initialize()
         aCalcConfig.SetStringRefSyntax( formula::FormulaGrammar::CONV_XL_A1 ) ;
         mpDoc->SetCalcConfig(aCalcConfig);
     }
-    else if (aGenerator.startsWithIgnoreAsciiCase("LibreOffice"))
+    // HST Office writes "HSTOffice/<release>$<OS>_<ARCH>" (hst-version-everywhere.patch): its own files
+    // keep their cached formula results like those of the engine it is built on
+    else if (aGenerator.startsWithIgnoreAsciiCase("LibreOffice")
+             || aGenerator.startsWithIgnoreAsciiCase("HSTOffice/"))
     {
         mbGeneratorKnownGood = true;
     }
